# The Rust that builds the app a Mac runs (desktop/scripts/pinned-cargo.sh,
# for stage-update.sh and install-app.sh): each of the three parts of
# rust-toolchain.toml's version, for each kind of Mac, by the SHA-256 of
# its .tar.xz and where Rust publishes it. pinned-cargo.sh downloads them
# itself and unpacks one only after its hash matches, so a compromised Rust
# distribution can't hand this Mac another compiler under that version
# number (Daybreak 173, 23 Nov 2026).
#
# The version must be rust-toolchain.toml's channel (a test checks). Moving
# it on: download https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/channel-rust-<version>.toml,
# check `shasum -a 256` of it matches the .sha256 beside it, and copy each
# [pkg.<part>.target.<target>] section's xz_hash and xz_url here, in the
# same commit as rust-toolchain.toml.
#
# version target part sha256 url
